This work identifies and classifies all possible AdS_4 spaces embedded in massive Type IIA, and categorizes them into five distinct groups based on their dual pairs. We have found that the AdS_4 with a non-zero H-flux can only arise from D6-branes in AdS_4 with no H-flux. Specifically, we have found the solutions belonging to the following dual pairs:

1. AdS_4 x S^6 and D6 x D0;
2. AdS_4 x S^2 x U(3) and D6 x D0;
3. Warped AdS_4 x S^2 and D6 x D4;
4. Half-BPS Warped AdS_4 x S^2 and D6 x D0;
5. Non-BPS Warped AdS_4 x S^2 and D6 x D0.

Notably, we have found that the solution belonging to the first pair in each of the last three pairs arises as a non-BPS Sasaki-Einstein reduction of its respective Fink-Thomas solution, which belongs to the first pair in the first identified group.
